hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19223","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman said, and I heard it from Harun: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Hurrah informed me from his uncle Hakim ibn Abi Hurrah from Sinan ibn Sannah, companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The grateful eater has like the reward of the patient faster."
"19224","Abdullah narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Hatim al-Tawil narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz al-Darawardi narrated to us the like of it."
"19225","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah narrated to us from Yahya ibn Hind that he heard Harmalah ibn Amr, and he is Abu Abd al-Rahman, who said: I performed the Farewell Hajj with my uncle Sinan ibn Sannah riding behind me. When we stood at Arafat I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placing one finger upon the other. I said to my uncle: What is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying? He said: He says: Stone the Jamrah with like the pebbles for flinging."
